ESCALATION (stands whatever the verdict) — no sanctioned red store

  What is left after the withdrawal is the mechanism, not the builder. The
  officina has nowhere to keep a per-behaviour red: ci/ holds gate logs keyed
  by source-tree hash, no CLI writes anything else there, and neither check
  nor verify knows a red exists. So a builder told to keep a red keeps it in
  /tmp, and a reviewer looking for one finds nothing and — as round 2 did —
  reads absence as never-produced. Both halves of that failure are the
  missing mechanism.

  W-019's reds are one `rm -rf /tmp` from gone; the durable copy is an
  untracked directory in one machine's home. The same answer W-016 waits on
  answers this: where a per-behaviour red lives, what writes it, and what
  check asserts about it. It should be answered once, for both.

ADVISORY 1 — two behaviours' reds are vacuous by construction

  Inside w019-red-docs.log, behaviours 7 and 10 ("checkDocs produces no
  findings for the repo as you leave it", "returns [] when opts.repo is
  omitted", "never throws on an empty root") pass against the stub — a
  behaviour that asserts an empty result is green against a function that
  returns nothing. Same for behaviour 5's determinism and write-scope
  assertions in w019-red-changelog.log. Not the builder's fault: a
  negative-space behaviour cannot go red against a stub, only against a
  mutant. 3c66190 shows the right shape — behaviour 3's red is a mutant that
  never converges. Whatever answer the Patron gives on the red store should
  say that a behaviour whose assertion is "nothing happens" records its red
  against a mutant, not a stub.

ADVISORY 2 — .claude/worktrees/ still not in .gitignore

  Round 2's advisory stands unchanged. It is in .git/info/exclude on this
  machine only, which is a per-session workaround. One line in .gitignore,
  alongside receipts/, sessions/, timeline/ and .bisellium/, which it
  belongs with for the same reason.

ADVISORY 3 — .lint-fix-test-* is the same class

  scripts/lint-fix.test.mjs mkdtemps `.lint-fix-test-*` at the repo root and
  removes it in a finally, which is right. Nothing ignores that pattern, so
  a crashed or killed run leaves an untracked directory and the next verify
  reports a dirty tree for a reason that has nothing to do with the source.
  Same one-line fix as ADVISORY 2, same .gitignore edit, next opus that owns
  the file.

ADVISORY 4 — no CLI moves an opus to done

  This verdict is recorded the only ways the CLI offers: a
  workflow.gate_evaluated emit for the review gate and a handoff on the
  traditio. Nothing in the CLI writes an agent gate's status into the opus's
  front matter or moves state: building -> done, and the standing rules
  forbid doing either by hand. Same family as the red-store gap, worth one
  answer with it.

